%N A183881 Number of arrangements of n+2 numbers in 0..6 with each number being the sum mod 7 of two others.
%H A183881 R. H. Hardin, <a href="/A183881/b183881.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..80</a>
%H A183881 <a href="/index/Rec#order_13">Index entries for linear recurrences with constant coefficients</a>, signature (29,-372,2812,-14030,48918,-122852,225316,-302121,292805,-199552,90648,-24624,3024).
%F A183881 From _Mikhail Smirnov_, Oct 23 2026: (Start)
%F A183881 a(n) = 7^(n+2) - (28*n^2 + 252*n + 554)*3^n + (9*n^3 + 201*n^2 + 1044*n + 1668)*2^(n-1) + 6*n^4 + 19*n^3 - 45*n^2 - 274*n - 342 for n >= 4.
%F A183881 G.f.: x * (1 - 28*x + 1574*x^2 - 5618*x^3 - 49422*x^4 + 369492*x^5 - 785698*x^6 - 161354*x^7 + 2990425*x^8 - 2608252*x^9 - 6884448*x^10 + 19679136*x^11 - 22752240*x^12 + 14453856*x^13 - 4966272*x^14 + 725760*x^15) / ((1 - x)^5 * (1 - 2*x)^4 * (1 - 3*x)^3 * (1 - 7*x)). (End)
